<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="santa-rosa-chick" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Chicken Salad - Santa Rosa</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup black rice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup lemon juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 chicken breasts, cooked and cubed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>4 green onions, finely sliced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 red bell pepper, diced (or 2)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 ounces pea pods, trimmed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium avocados, diced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup pecans, chopped and toasted</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><xref ref="vinaigrette">Vinaigrette Dressing</xref> (with rice vinegar and canola oil)</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Early in the day, prepare rice, chicken, onions, bell pepper, and pea pods.  These can then be combined or just placed in a bowl together to toss before serving.  Cover and refrigerate.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Chop and toast the pecans and place them in a ziplock bag to add just before serving.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Just before serving, add the avocados, lemon juice, and dressing.  Sprinkle with pecans, or serve pecans on the side.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          For the dressing, use only <m>\frac{1}{3}</m> cup canola oil.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>